## Key Gaps

### 1. Backend Model Missing Fields
The frontend `Task` type has fields the backend model doesn't:
- `phase_id` — which phase/visit the task belongs to
- `assigned_role` — role-based assignment (PI, CRC, Nurse, etc.)
- `blocked_reason` — structured JSON for blocker metadata
- `blocked_since` — when the task was blocked
- `order_in_phase` — display ordering
- `suggested_date` — AI-suggested due date
- `suggested_assignee` — AI-suggested person

### 2. Dependencies Not Stored
The frontend has a full dependency system (`TaskDependency` with source/target/type), but the backend has no `task_dependencies` table. The `mapRouter.ts` stubs return empty arrays.

### 3. Mock Phases
The `mapRouter.ts` generates 4 hardcoded phases (Screening, Baseline, Treatment, Follow-up) instead of reading from the backend. Real phase management doesn't exist in the backend.

